<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Debug-only additions. Never merged into a release build, so nothing here can ship.

    MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE exists for one reason: the summarisation benchmark needs to read a
    multi-gigabyte model file that cannot live in the app's own directory. The isolated instrumented
    build is uninstalled after every run, which would take a 2.6 GB model and the report with it —
    so both sit in shared storage instead, and reading them from there needs this.

    It is inert until granted, and granting is a deliberate adb command:

        adb shell appops set com.baba.callvault.instrtest MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE allow

    The real app has never asked for this and must not: it reaches recordings through the folders
    the user picked, which is the whole point of using the Storage Access Framework.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <uses-permission
        android:name="android.permission.MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE"
        tools:ignore="ScopedStorage" />

</manifest>
